MIRA Data Processing Brief

Prepared for: Data Protection Officer / legal counsel
System: MIRA Project 3 MVP
Assessment date: 18 August 2026

1. Does MIRA process personal data?

Yes. MIRA processes information relating to an identifiable user and may also process information about other identifiable people shown in uploaded reference images. Questionnaire answers, free text, uploaded photographs, the user’s name or contact details, technical identifiers, and AI-derived Creative DNA or personality/brand attributes are personal data. Pseudonymous IDs remain personal data while MIRA or a vendor can reconnect them to the user.

The generated profile, shoot plan, moodboard, and images are also personal data when they relate to or portray an identifiable user. The MVP does not use anonymised data only.

